# world.kb — more countries, and the organisations, landmarks and lines that span them.
#
# `geography.kb` carries about forty countries with their capitals and currencies, which is the
# right shape and not enough of it, and it stops at the border: the United Nations gets one line
# in `society.kb` and nothing else that operates between countries has an entry at all. So "what
# is the WHO", "where is Machu Picchu", "what is the Commonwealth" and half the countries on the
# map had no answer.
#
# `capital` and `currency` are functional — one value each — so a country appears here only if it
# is not already in `geography.kb`, and the two files never state the same pair twice.

