# --- what a country is made of ----------------------------------------------------------------------- #
nation | is_a=group of people | means=a people who see themselves as one community | has_property=not the same thing as a state
state | is_a=political entity | means=an organised political community under one government | has_part=territory | has_part=population | has_part=government
border | is_a=boundary | means=the line where one country's territory ends and another's begins | causes=customs and passport checks
passport | is_a=document | purpose=identifying a traveller and their nationality | requires=being issued by a government
visa | is_a=permission | purpose=allowing a foreigner to enter a country for a stated reason and time
citizenship | is_a=status | means=full membership of a state, with its rights and duties | requires=birth, descent or naturalisation
capital city | means=the city where a country's government sits
national flag | is_a=symbol | purpose=standing for a country | has_property=its colours and emblems usually carry a stated meaning
national anthem | is_a=song | purpose=standing for a country at formal occasions
sovereignty | is_a=principle | means=a state's authority over its own territory being final | causes=other states having no right to rule inside it
colonialism | is_a=historical system | means=one country ruling and exploiting another people's territory | causes=borders drawn without regard to the people inside them
independence | is_a=event | means=a territory becoming a sovereign state | occurs_when=colonial rule ends

# --- organisations between countries ------------------------------------------------------------------- #
international organisation | is_a=institution | means=a body whose members are states | has_kind=United Nations | has_kind=World Health Organization | has_kind=World Trade Organization
World Health Organization | is_a=international organisation | purpose=coordinating international public health | part_of=United Nations | located_in=Geneva | also_known_as=WHO
UNICEF | is_a=international organisation | purpose=protecting the rights and welfare of children | part_of=United Nations
UNESCO | is_a=international organisation | purpose=cooperation in education, science and culture | part_of=United Nations | involves=World Heritage Sites
World Trade Organization | is_a=international organisation | purpose=setting and enforcing the rules of trade between countries
International Monetary Fund | is_a=international organisation | purpose=lending to countries in financial difficulty and monitoring the world economy
World Bank | is_a=international organisation | purpose=lending for development projects in poorer countries
Security Council | is_a=body | part_of=United Nations | purpose=deciding on matters of international peace and security | has_property=five permanent members with a veto
General Assembly | is_a=body | part_of=United Nations | purpose=where every member state has one vote
International Court of Justice | is_a=court | purpose=settling legal disputes between states | located_in=The Hague
European Union | is_a=international organisation | means=a union of European states with a single market | has_part=European Parliament | causes=free movement of goods and people among members
NATO | is_a=alliance | purpose=collective defence among its members | has_property=an attack on one is treated as an attack on all
Commonwealth of Nations | is_a=international organisation | means=an association of states, most of them formerly under British rule
ASEAN | is_a=international organisation | located_in=Southeast Asia | purpose=economic and political cooperation among its members
BRICS | is_a=group of countries | means=a grouping of major emerging economies | involves=Brazil, Russia, India, China and South Africa
G20 | is_a=group of countries | purpose=coordinating on the world economy | has_property=its members produce most of the world's output
OPEC | is_a=international organisation | purpose=coordinating the petroleum policies of its member countries
Red Cross | is_a=organisation | purpose=humanitarian relief in war and disaster | has_property=neutral by charter
Amnesty International | is_a=organisation | purpose=campaigning for human rights
Greenpeace | is_a=organisation | purpose=campaigning on environmental issues
Nobel Prize | is_a=prize | purpose=recognising outstanding contributions in named fields | located_in=Sweden | has_kind=Nobel Prize in Literature | has_kind=Nobel Peace Prize
Nobel Peace Prize | is_a=Nobel Prize | purpose=recognising work for peace | located_in=Norway
World Heritage Site | is_a=designation | purpose=marking a place of outstanding value to humanity | requires=listing by UNESCO

# --- landmarks and lines on the map ------------------------------------------------------------------------ #
Machu Picchu | is_a=archaeological site | located_in=Peru | is_a=World Heritage Site | has_property=an Inca city high in the Andes
Petra | is_a=archaeological site | located_in=Jordan | has_property=buildings carved into rose coloured rock
Stonehenge | is_a=monument | located_in=England | has_property=a prehistoric ring of standing stones
Eiffel Tower | is_a=monument | located_in=Paris | consists_of=wrought iron | has_property=built for a world fair
Statue of Liberty | is_a=monument | located_in=New York | purpose=a gift from France marking friendship and liberty
Christ the Redeemer | is_a=monument | located_in=Rio de Janeiro
Angkor Wat | is_a=temple | located_in=Cambodia | has_property=the largest religious monument in the world
Forbidden City | is_a=palace complex | located_in=Beijing | purpose=the imperial seat of Ming and Qing China
Acropolis | is_a=archaeological site | located_in=Athens | has_part=Parthenon
Sydney Opera House | is_a=building | located_in=Sydney | has_property=a roof of shell shaped shapes
Niagara Falls | is_a=waterfall | located_in=the border of Canada and the United States
Angel Falls | is_a=waterfall | located_in=Venezuela | has_property=the highest uninterrupted waterfall
Dead Sea | is_a=lake | has_property=the lowest land surface on Earth | has_property=so salty that people float
Lake Baikal | is_a=lake | located_in=Russia | has_property=the deepest lake in the world
Caspian Sea | is_a=lake | has_property=the largest inland body of water
Suez Canal | is_a=canal | located_in=Egypt | purpose=linking the Mediterranean and the Red Sea | causes=a far shorter route between Europe and Asia
Panama Canal | is_a=canal | located_in=Panama | purpose=linking the Atlantic and the Pacific | has_part=lock
Tropic of Cancer | is_a=line of latitude | means=the northern limit of where the Sun can be overhead
Tropic of Capricorn | is_a=line of latitude | means=the southern limit of where the Sun can be overhead
Arctic Circle | is_a=line of latitude | means=the line north of which the Sun does not set at midsummer
hemisphere | is_a=half of the Earth | has_kind=northern hemisphere | has_kind=southern hemisphere | means=half the globe, divided by the equator or a meridian
archipelago | is_a=landform | means=a group or chain of islands
strait | is_a=waterway | means=a narrow channel of water joining two larger bodies
isthmus | is_a=landform | means=a narrow strip of land joining two larger land masses
delta of a river | is_a=landform | occurs_when=a river drops its sediment as it meets the sea | has_property=very fertile
oasis | is_a=place | means=a fertile spot in a desert where groundwater reaches the surface
